cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CyanoTools in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "CyanoTools – a web-based toolkit for cyanobacteria, algae, and plants research"
abstract: >-
  CyanoTools is a free, open-access, browser-based platform for processing and
  analysing data from cyanobacteria, microalgae and higher plants. It covers PAM
  fluorometry (rapid light curves, OJIP transients, Kautsky kinetics, sigma(II)),
  fluorescence spectroscopy and excitation-emission matrices, membrane inlet mass
  spectrometry, microscopy image analysis (cell counting, cell size, morphology,
  pigment profiles), photobioreactor growth analysis, genome-scale metabolic
  modelling, statistics and wet-lab calculators. Raw instrument files go in,
  publication-ready spreadsheets and plots come out. No installation, no account,
  and no server-side retention of user data.
type: software
